---
layout: base.njk
title: "Nirmaan — You bring the problem. We build the system."
description: "Websites, apps, automation, AI and custom business software. Tell Nirmaan the problem; we'll work out and build the system you actually need."
ogDescription: "You bring the problem. We build the system. Websites, apps, automation, AI systems and custom software for real businesses."
permalink: "/"
scripts: ["hero.js"]
nav: "home"
cta:
  eyebrow: "No spec needed"
  lines: ["Tell us the problem.", "We'll work out the system."]
  text: "You don't need to know whether you need a website, an app or an automation. Describe what's going wrong, and we'll reply within 24 hours with honest thoughts on approach, timeline and budget."
  primary: { label: "Tell us your problem", href: "/contact.html" }
  secondary: { label: "See pricing", href: "/pricing.html" }
layers:
  - { name: "Database", tech: "PostgreSQL · MySQL", text: "Structured storage designed around your data, not bolted on later. Fast to query, backed up, secured." }
  - { name: "Backend logic", tech: "Node.js · Python", text: "The rules only your business has: pricing, approvals, calculations, workflows. Written as real code, not plugins." }
  - { name: "APIs & integrations", tech: "REST · Payments · Webhooks", text: "Clean interfaces between your system and everything it talks to: payment gateways, CRMs, messaging, partners." }
  - { name: "Automation", tech: "Schedules · Triggers · Reports", text: "The repetitive work nobody should do by hand. Imports, notifications, reports and syncs that just run." }
  - { name: "Interface", tech: "HTML · React · Next.js", text: "The website or app your customers and staff actually touch. Fast, accessible and mobile-first." }
principles:
  - { glyph: "11111/10001/10101/10001/11111", title: "Built for you, not templated", text: "No page builders or themes stretched to fit. Every project is designed and coded for your specific goals." }
  - { glyph: "11111/00000/11111/00000/11111", title: "Full stack, one team", text: "Frontend, backend, database and APIs under one roof, so nothing gets lost between vendors." }
  - { glyph: "01110/01010/01010/01010/01110", title: "Fast on every screen", text: "Mobile-first layouts and lean code that load quickly on the phones your customers actually use." }
  - { glyph: "00001/00011/01011/11011/11111", title: "Measured by business results", text: "We optimise for enquiries, conversions, speed and security, not for how the portfolio shot looks." }
  - { glyph: "11011/11011/00000/11011/11011", title: "Clean, handover-ready code", text: "Modular, documented code you own outright, simple for us or anyone else to extend later." }
  - { glyph: "01110/10001/10101/10001/01110", title: "Here after launch", text: "Maintenance, improvements and new features as you grow. We don't disappear at go-live." }
journey:
  - { title: "Discover", text: "Your business, the people affected, and what solved looks like.", stamp: "problem understood" }
  - { title: "Plan", text: "Scope, architecture and one fixed price.", stamp: "requirements confirmed", approve: true }
  - { title: "Design", text: "Screens and flows you can click through.", stamp: "system designed", approve: true }
  - { title: "Build", text: "Frontend, backend, APIs and database, properly tested.", stamp: "built and tested" }
  - { title: "Launch", text: "Deployed, monitored and improved after go-live.", stamp: "live and monitored", approve: true }
tools: ["HTML5", "Modern CSS", "JavaScript", "React", "Next.js", "Node.js", "Python", "REST APIs", "PostgreSQL", "MySQL", "Git", "Cloud hosting"]
---
{#- ============================================================
    HERO
============================================================ #}
<section class="hero" data-hero aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <canvas class="hero__canvas" data-hero-canvas aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div class="hero__grid-fallback" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="wrap hero__inner">
    <div class="hero__copy">
      <p class="hero__meaning">Software studio</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title display" id="hero-title">
        <span class="line"><span>You bring</span></span>
        <span class="line"><span>the problem.</span></span>
        <span class="line"><span class="accent">We build</span></span>
        <span class="line"><span class="accent">the system.</span></span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede hero__lede">Websites, apps, automation, AI and custom business software, turning <strong>real-world problems into reliable systems</strong>.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact.html">Tell us your problem {% glyph "00100/00010/11111/00010/00100", "btn__arrow" %}</a>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="#process">How it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero__side">
      <div class="hero__slot" data-hero-slot>
        {% logo "hero__mark-fallback" %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- set capabilities = ["Websites", "Web applications", "Mobile apps", "Internal tools", "Dashboards", "Workflow automation", "AI systems", "Integrations", "Business portals", "SaaS products", "Data systems", "Modernisation"] %}
  <div class="ticker" aria-label="What we build">
    <div class="ticker__track">
      <ul class="ticker__list" role="list">
        {%- for c in capabilities %}<li>{{ c }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <ul class="ticker__list" role="list" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- for c in capabilities %}<li>{{ c }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- ============================================================
    WHAT'S INSIDE: the layer stack (pinned on wide screens)
============================================================ #}
<section class="stack" id="inside" data-scene="stack" aria-labelledby="inside-title">
  <div class="stack__sticky">
    <div class="wrap stack__grid">
      <div class="stack__intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">What a Nirmaan build contains</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="inside-title">Not just the front&nbsp;end.</h2>
        <p class="section__text">Most studios hand over a website. We build what sits underneath it too: five layers, one system, one team accountable for all of it.</p>
        <div class="stack__meter" data-meter aria-hidden="true">
          {%- for l in layers %}<span></span>{% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="mono stack__count" data-stack-count aria-hidden="true">{{ layers | length }} / {{ layers | length }}</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="tower" role="list" aria-label="The layers of a build, from the ground up">
        {%- for l in layers %}
        <li class="layer" data-layer>
          <div class="layer__head">
            <span class="layer__name">{{ l.name }}</span>
            <span class="layer__tech">{{ l.tech }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="layer__body"><p>{{ l.text }}</p></div>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- ============================================================
    SERVICES RAIL (horizontal on vertical scroll)
============================================================ #}
<section class="rail" id="services" data-scene="rail" aria-labelledby="services-title">
  <div class="rail__sticky">
    <div class="wrap rail__head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What we build</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="services-title">Whatever the problem needs.</h2>
      </div>
      <a class="link-arrow" href="/services.html">All {{ services | serviceCount }} services <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>

    <div class="rail__viewport" data-rail-viewport>
      <ul class="rail__track" data-rail-track role="list">
        {%- for f in services.featured %}
        {%- set s = services | service(f.id) %}
        <li>
          <a class="svc-card" href="/services/{{ f.id }}.html">
            {% glyph s.glyph, "svc-card__glyph" %}
            <div>
              <h3 class="svc-card__title" data-morph="svc-{{ f.id }}">{{ f.title }}</h3>
              <p class="svc-card__text">{{ f.text }}</p>
              <p class="svc-card__more">Details →</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
        <li>
          <a class="svc-card svc-card--all" href="/services.html">
            <div>
              <h3 class="svc-card__title">See the full catalogue</h3>
              <p class="svc-card__text">{{ services | serviceCount }} services across websites, applications, AI, mobile and integrations.</p>
              <p class="svc-card__more">Services →</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap"><div class="rail__progress" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- ============================================================
    CLIENT WORK
============================================================ #}
<section class="section case" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
  <div class="wrap case__grid">
    <div class="case__intro" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Client work · Sudaangeo.in</p>
      <h2 class="case__title display" id="work-title">Came for a website. Left with an&nbsp;engine.</h2>
      <div class="actions case__actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/projects.html">Read the case study {% glyph "00100/00010/11111/00010/00100", "btn__arrow" %}</a>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="https://sudaangeo.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit the live site <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="case__body" data-reveal style="--d: 1">
      <p>Sudaangeo asked us for a website. What we built was a data-processing and business-automation tool that now runs a real part of their day-to-day operations.</p>
      <p>The public site is only the visible layer. Behind it sit custom backend logic, a real database and automated workflows, all shaped around how Sudaangeo actually works.</p>
      <ol class="scope" role="list" aria-label="What we delivered">
        <li><span class="mono">Layer 1</span><span class="scope__name">Public website</span><span class="scope__text">Brand presence and the front door to the system.</span></li>
        <li><span class="mono">Layer 2</span><span class="scope__name">Backend &amp; database</span><span class="scope__text">Custom logic over a structured data model.</span></li>
        <li><span class="mono">Layer 3</span><span class="scope__name">Data-processing engine</span><span class="scope__text">Automation that replaced manual operational work.</span></li>
        <li><span class="mono">Layer 4</span><span class="scope__name">Ongoing support</span><span class="scope__text">Iteration as the business keeps changing.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- ============================================================
    PRINCIPLES + TOOLS
============================================================ #}
<section class="section" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why Nirmaan</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="why-title">Built around your business, not a&nbsp;template.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__text">Clean code, direct communication with the people building it, and full-stack execution from first call to long after launch.</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="principles" role="list" data-swipe aria-label="Why Nirmaan">
      {%- for p in principles %}
      <li data-reveal style="--d: {{ loop.index0 % 3 }}">
        {% glyph p.glyph %}
        <h3>{{ p.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ p.text }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>

    <div class="toolbelt" data-reveal>
      <p class="mono">Tools we use daily</p>
      <ul class="tags" role="list">
        {%- for t in tools %}<li>{{ t }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <a class="link-arrow" href="/technology.html">Full stack <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- ============================================================
    PROCESS
============================================================ #}
<section class="section" id="process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="process-title">Five steps. No&nbsp;surprises.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__text">You approve the plan and the design before we build, and you always know where things stand. <a href="/process.html">See every deliverable</a>.</p>
    </div>

    {#- Problem → system, told as a pinned scene (site.js, [data-scene="build"]):
        the customer's words become a system, as you scroll. Written in its
        finished state, so without motion it is a before-and-after. #}
    <div class="build" data-scene="build">
      <div class="build__sticky">
        <div class="build__grid">
          <ol class="build__beats" role="list">
            <li data-span="0 0.28"><span class="mono">It starts in your words</span><p class="journey__quote display">“We keep losing orders in&nbsp;WhatsApp.”</p></li>
            <li data-span="0.28 0.5"><span class="mono">We find the structure</span><p>Every order is a customer, items and a date. The one that slipped through has no record at all.</p></li>
            <li data-span="0.5 0.8"><span class="mono">We build the system</span><p>Orders land in one place, each with a status, instead of scrolling away in a chat.</p></li>
            <li data-span="0.8 1.01"><span class="mono">Your team runs on it</span><p>Everyone sees what's due, and nothing is lost.</p></li>
          </ol>

          <figure class="build__stage">
            <div class="chat">
              <p class="build__label mono">Before: orders in a chat</p>
              <ul class="chat__list" role="list">
            <li class="msg" data-at="0.04 0.08">
              <span class="msg__who">Ravi Traders <time class="mono">9:02</time></span>
              <span class="msg__text">Need <mark data-at="0.30 0.34">20 kg basmati rice</mark> by <mark data-at="0.31 0.35">Friday</mark></span>
            </li>
            <li class="msg" data-at="0.08 0.12">
              <span class="msg__who">Meena Stores <time class="mono">9:15</time></span>
              <span class="msg__text">Same as last week: <mark data-at="0.33 0.37">12 packs atta</mark>, deliver <mark data-at="0.34 0.38">Thursday</mark></span>
            </li>
            <li class="msg" data-at="0.12 0.16">
              <span class="msg__who">Hotel Sagar <time class="mono">9:31</time></span>
              <span class="msg__text">Please send <mark data-at="0.36 0.40">8 L cooking oil</mark> <mark data-at="0.37 0.41">tomorrow</mark></span>
            </li>
            <li class="msg" data-at="0.16 0.20">
              <span class="msg__who">Ravi Traders <time class="mono">10:05</time></span>
              <span class="msg__text">Also add <mark data-at="0.39 0.43">5 kg dal</mark> to my order</span>
            </li>
            <li class="msg msg--lost" data-at="0.20 0.24">
              <span class="msg__who">Anand Kirana <time class="mono">10:20</time></span>
              <span class="msg__text">Did you get my order from Monday??</span>
              <span class="msg__flag" data-at="0.43 0.47">No record of this order</span>
            </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="sys">
              <p class="build__label mono">After: one orders system</p>
              <table class="orders">
                <thead><tr><th scope="col">Order</th><th scope="col">Customer</th><th scope="col">Items</th><th scope="col">Due</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
              <tr data-at="0.52 0.56" data-states='[[0.52,"new"],[0.82,"confirmed"]]'>
                <td class="mono">#1041</td><td>Ravi Traders</td><td>20 kg basmati rice, 5 kg dal</td><td>Fri</td>
                <td><span class="order__state" data-state="confirmed">confirmed</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr data-at="0.56 0.60" data-states='[[0.56,"new"],[0.84,"confirmed"]]'>
                <td class="mono">#1042</td><td>Meena Stores</td><td>12 packs atta</td><td>Thu</td>
                <td><span class="order__state" data-state="confirmed">confirmed</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr data-at="0.60 0.64" data-states='[[0.60,"new"],[0.86,"confirmed"]]'>
                <td class="mono">#1043</td><td>Hotel Sagar</td><td>8 L cooking oil</td><td>Tomorrow</td>
                <td><span class="order__state" data-state="confirmed">confirmed</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr data-at="0.64 0.68" data-states='[[0.64,"new"],[0.88,"follow up"]]'>
                <td class="mono">#1044</td><td>Anand Kirana</td><td>Monday's order</td><td>Today</td>
                <td><span class="order__state" data-state="follow up">follow up</span></td>
              </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
              <ul class="tiles" role="list">
                <li data-at="0.90 0.94"><b>4</b> open orders</li>
                <li data-at="0.92 0.96"><b>3</b> due by Friday</li>
                <li data-at="0.94 0.98"><b>0</b> lost in chat</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <figcaption class="mono">Illustration: a typical problem, and the kind of system we build for it.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline timeline--journey" data-scene="line">
      <span class="timeline__bar" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <ol class="timeline__list" role="list">
        {%- for st in journey %}
        <li>
          <span class="mono">Step {{ loop.index }}</span>
          <h3>{{ st.title }}</h3>
          <p>{{ st.text }}</p>
          <span class="stamp{% if st.approve %} stamp--approve{% endif %}"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> {{ st.stamp }}</span>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <p class="journey__to" data-reveal>
      <span class="mono">It ends with</span>
      <span>A system your team runs on. <b>You approve every key step</b>, so nothing is built that you didn't agree to.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{#- ============================================================
    PACKAGES
============================================================ #}
<section class="section" id="packages" aria-labelledby="packages-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="packages-title">Honest prices, fixed before we&nbsp;start.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__text">Starting prices below. Your project gets one fixed quote after a free conversation, paid in three steps as it progresses. <a href="/pricing.html">Full pricing, care plans and an estimator</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="packages packages--4" role="list" data-swipe aria-label="Packages">
      {%- for p in pricing.packages %}
      <li class="package{% if p.highlight %} package--featured{% endif %}" data-reveal style="--d: {{ loop.index0 }}">
        {% glyph p.glyph, "package__glyph" %}
        <div>
          <h3 class="package__name"><a href="/pricing/{{ p.id }}.html" data-morph="plan-{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }}</a></h3>
          <p class="package__for">{{ p.for }}</p>
          <p class="package__price"><span>from</span><b>{{ p.from | inr }}</b></p>
        </div>
        <ul class="ticks" role="list">
          {%- for f in p.features | batch(3) | first %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <a class="btn{% if not p.highlight %} btn--ghost{% endif %}" href="/pricing/{{ p.id }}.html">See what's in {{ p.name }}<span class="visually-hidden"> (from {{ p.from | inr }})</span></a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
